The reference MBPP problem: harmonic_sum(n) returns 1/n + harmonic_sum(n-1) with base case n<2 returning 1. The standard solution is:

def harmonic_sum(n):
  if n < 2:
    return 1
  else:
    return 1 / n + (harmonic_sum(n - 1))

The test harmonic_sum(7) = 2.5928571428571425, which is H_7 = 2.592857..., so it matches the candidate.

The candidate is identical to the reference solution. Other tests are likely harmonic_sum(4) = 2.083333 and harmonic_sum(10) = 2.9289682539682538, both of which equal H_n, so the candidate passes.

